for the old winning `tf1/r1` (29\times29) minor, whose omitted input shift was $r_c=7$. It is neither the value nor a bound for $L_s^+$. The artifact `delta_plus_eta29` is also not a corrected square truncation: it is a $(29N+1)\times29N$ matrix that still omits the selected input. Strictly, no promoted DEPTH $e$ existed even before this correction. Preserve `295` only under a name such as `OLD_29MINOR_E_INDEX`; do not use the derived target $D=591$.

