   497	## 3. The radical-fiber group
   498	
   499	### 3.1 The 36-point torsor
   500	
   501	At either split prime, fix the chosen square root `r` of 3 and a primitive
   502	cube root `omega`.  The selector algebra is
   503	
   504	\[
   505	B_{36}=\mathbb F_p[A_1,A_2,h_1,h_2]/
   506	\left(A_1^3-(3+r),A_2^3-(3-r),2h_1^2-3,2h_2^2-3\right)
   507	\simeq\mathbb F_p^{36}.\tag{3.1}
   508	\]
   509	
   510	Here `h_i=HW_i/W_i`.  Its components are labeled
   511	
   512	```text
   513	a{i}{j}{s1}{s2},     i,j in Z/3,     s1,s2 in {p,m}.
   514	```
   515	
   516	Define
   517	
   518	\[
   519	G=(\mathbb Z/3)^2\times(\mathbb Z/2)^2
   520	\]
   521	
   522	and, for `g=(a,b,e1,e2)`, let
   523	
   524	\[
   525	g:(i,j,s_1,s_2)\longmapsto
   526	(i+a,j+b,(-1)^{e_1}s_1,(-1)^{e_2}s_2).\tag{3.2}
   527	\]
   528	
   529	Equivalently on selectors,
   530	
   531	\[
   532	(A_1,A_2,h_1,h_2)\longmapsto
   533	(\omega^aA_1,\omega^bA_2,(-1)^{e_1}h_1,(-1)^{e_2}h_2).\tag{3.3}
   534	\]
   535	
   536	The action is free and transitive, so the 36 points form one `G`-torsor.
   537	
   538	For `p=105337`, exact atlas data give
   539	
   540	\[
   541	\omega=15094,\quad\omega^2=90242,
   542	\]
   543	
   544	and the `a00pp` selector point is
   545	
   546	\[
   547	(A_1,A_2,h_1,h_2)=(50630,10114,50267,50267).\tag{3.4}
   548	\]
   549	
   550	Every JSON fiber is exactly
   551	
   552	\[
   553	(\omega^iA_1,\omega^jA_2,s_1h_1,s_2h_2).
