   852	> defined and 42 is invertible, the residue-A, fixed-`r`, `B`-frozen,
   853	> no-log, `PIN42`, `W`-chart depth ideal is `G`-equivariant at every
   854	> truncation depth.  Its 36 radical fibers are one orbit of isomorphic
   855	> schemes.
   856	
   857	Adjoining `zeta` is a proof device: the branch permutation descends to the
   858	displayed `omega` and sign scalings on the invariant coefficient objects.
   859	
   860	### 5.3 Consequences for banked algebraic operations
   861	
   862	Let `D_g` be the diagonal coordinate matrix of `T_g` and `E_g` the row
   863	matrix in (5.4).
   864	
   865	1. **Groebner bases and normal forms.** Diagonal scaling preserves every
   866	   monomial and the monomial order.  Uniqueness of a reduced monic basis
   867	   implies that the target basis is the transformed source basis followed
   868	   by leading-coefficient normalization.  Leading monomials and
   869	   elementwise supports are therefore identical.  This explains the
   870	   397-element D21 and 509-element D23 atlas support identities.  Normal
   871	   forms commute with transport.
   872	
   873	2. **Jacobians and minors.** Differentiating
   874	   `F_{g lambda}(D_g x)=E_g F_lambda(x)` gives
   875	   \[
   876	   J_{g\lambda}(D_gx)D_g=E_gJ_\lambda(x).\tag{5.5}
   877	   \]
   878	   Ranks, tangent/conormal dimensions, and determinantal conditions are
   879	   unchanged.
   880	
   881	3. **Schur and pivot operations.** Affine blocks acquire only invertible
   882	   diagonal row and column factors.  Unit pivots, ranks, left kernels,
   883	   compatibility rows, and backsolves transport.
   884	
   885	4. **Saturation.** For the induced ring automorphism `S_g`,
   886	   \[
   887	   S_g(I:q^\infty)=S_g(I):(S_gq)^\infty.\tag{5.6}
   888	   \]
   889	   The annihilator must itself be transported; one must not reuse the same
   890	   printed coefficients on a different fiber.
   891	
   892	5. **Witnesses.** Since `omega` and `±1` lie in each split prime field,
   893	   every banked `a00pp` rational witness transports to rational witnesses
   894	   on the other 35 fibers.  Transporting the six D23 witnesses and checking
   895	   the first 29 equations gave 216 fiber-witness checks per prime, all zero
   896	   (432 total).
   897	
   898	These statements concern algebraic presentations at a fixed finite depth.
   899	They do not prove DEPTH-STAB, a Hensel condition, existence of an inverse
   900	limit point, algebraization, or a polynomial Keller pair.
