    92	## Exact scope of “one fiber decides all 36”
    93	
    94	This is the consequence the rest of the campaign will try to spend.
    95	State it as a theorem with its actual hypotheses, not as a slogan.
    96	
    97	**What one `a00pp` verdict plus equivariance does decide.**
    98	Fix one banked split prime, one square root of 3, the residue-A
    99	`B`-frozen no-log `PIN42` \(W\)-chart, and a presentation \(I(\lambda)\)
   100	of the depth-\(D\) ideal on fiber \(\lambda\) that is related to the
   101	pristine source by a character-semi-invariant exact localization
   102	(the parked D25 systems are in this class; a reduced monic GB of an
   103	equivariant ideal is in this class). Let \(T_g\in\mathrm{GL}_{28}(\mathbf F_p)\)
   104	be the diagonal scaling of §4.2. Then
   105	
   106	\[
   107	T_g^*I(g\lambda)=I(\lambda),
   108	\]
   109	
   110	so \(\mathbf F_p[x]/I(\lambda)\cong\mathbf F_p[x]/I(g\lambda)\) as
   111	\(\mathbf F_p\)-algebras. Every isomorphism invariant is therefore
   112	constant on the 36 fibers, **including dimension**:
   113	
   114	- emptiness / `NONEMPTY` over \(\mathbf F_p\) and over
   115	  \(\overline{\mathbf F}_p\);
   116	- Krull dimension of the affine scheme (arithmetic and geometric);
   117	- degree, Hilbert function, leading-term ideal of a reduced GB
   118	  (diagonal scaling preserves monomials and any monomial order;
   119	  only leading-coefficient normalization is needed);
   120	- Jacobian / conormal ranks, determinantal rank defects;
   121	- existence of a point over \(\mathbf F_p\) or over an extension
   122	  (an \(\mathbf F_p\)-point transports to an \(\mathbf F_p\)-point
   123	  by \(T_g\), because \(T_g\) is \(\mathbf F_p\)-rational);
   124	- component count after the corresponding base change.
   125	
   126	Empirically this already matches the atlas: at both primes, all 36
   127	fibers have `d21 dim = 13`, `det23 dim = 11`, `n_basis = 397/509`,
   128	`cond_dim = 3`, `nf_rank = 5`, verdict `NONEMPTY`. Those numbers are
   129	not an extra miracle; they are the theorem plus GB uniqueness.
   130	
   131	**The scalings are \(\mathbf F_p\)-rational.** They do **not** live
   132	in an extension. Verified:
   133	
   134	- \(p\in\{105337,105673\}\), both \(\equiv 1\pmod{12}\), both
   135	  \(42\mid(p-1)\).
   136	- \(\bigl(\frac{3}{p}\bigr)=1\). Square roots of 3 exist in
   137	  \(\mathbf F_p\) (Tonelli: 795 and 14686 for the atlas's choice of
   138	  \(r\)). This puts the **selector points** on \(\mathbf F_p\), and
   139	  is why the 36 fibers are \(\mathbf F_p\)-rational points of
   140	  \(B_{36}\). It is **not** what makes \(T_g\) rational.
   141	- Primitive cube roots exist in \(\mathbf F_p\) (full scan, two
   142	  each): \(\omega=15094,\;\omega^2=90242\) at 105337;
   143	  \(\omega=13168,\;\omega^2=92504\) at 105673. These are exactly the
   144	  document's values. \(\omega^2+\omega+1=0\), \(\omega^3=1\),
   145	  \(\omega\neq 1\).
   146	- Every diagonal entry of every \(T_g\) is in
   147	  \(\{1,-1,\omega,\omega^2,-\omega,-\omega^2\}\subset\mathbf F_p^\times\).
   148	  \(\sqrt{3}\) never appears in \(T_g\). Sign characters are
   149	  \(\pm 1\in\mathbf F_p\).
   150	
   151	Consequently the transport is an isomorphism of affine
   152	\(\mathbf F_p\)-schemes. It is **not** “only over the closure.”
   153	(If these primes had failed to contain \(\omega\), geometric
   154	dimension would still match after \(\mathbf F_p(\omega)/\mathbf F_p\),
   155	but \(\mathbf F_p\)-points and arithmetic invariants would not
   156	automatically transport. That is not this bank: \(\omega\in\mathbf F_p\).
   157	Separately, \(\zeta_{42}\) also lies in both fields, so the source
   158	proof's cyclotomic device does not leave \(\mathbf F_p\) either at
   159	these two primes.)
   160	
   161	**What one fiber does not decide.**
   162	
   163	1. A future optimized D27+ presentation obtained by pivoting, Schur
   164	   reduction, saturation, or fiber-dependent gauges, unless it
   165	   passes FUTURE-EMISSION FIDELITY. Copying printed coefficients
   166	   onto another fiber is false (saturation identity (5.6); the
   167	   annihilator must be transported). This gap is operational and
   168	   finite, and is already the document's gate, not a hidden hole
   169	   in the theorem.
   170	2. The other \(\sqrt{3}\) embedding. The two \(r\)'s are not in
   171	   the same \(G\)-orbit.
   172	3. The other prime. \(|G|=36\) does not mix 105337 with 105673.
   173	   The honest reduction is \(36\to 1\) per prime and \(72\to 2\)
   174	   across the bank, as written in (6.2).
   175	4. Unfrozen `B`, log chart, other infinity charts, pole-chart
   176	   swap. No action is claimed.
   177	5. DEPTH-STAB, Hensel, an inverse-limit point, algebraization, or
   178	   a polynomial Keller pair. Equivariance of a finite-depth
   179	   obstruction is not a germ.
   180	6. Numerical coefficient arrays themselves. Invariants match;
   181	   coordinates of a witness map by \(T_g\) and are not equal as
   182	   tuples.
   183	
   184	**Bottom line for the campaign.** For every faithful emitted system
   185	at one of these two primes, one representative solve plus 35
   186	explicit diagonal transports replaces 36 solves, **and that includes
   187	dimension**. The parked D25 systems are faithful in this sense
   188	(character identity checked). A compiler that silently breaks
   189	homogeneity does not get the 36× for free.
