xmodel/sol-lateral.md:316:2. Prove a separate realization lemma: a resolved Puiseux cone plus specified angular-component, codimension, and overlap data determines a measurable \(p\)-adic cylinder of measure \((1-q^{-1})^r q^{-\ell(n)}\). A bare valuation vector is not enough.
xmodel/sol-lateral.md:323:Kill if the realization/change-of-variables bridge fails, or if the promoted tower records do not determine angular components, codimension, Jacobian order, and disjointness without essentially reconstructing the entire polynomial map. Also kill if the full generating function formally collapses to \(td=\sum\Lambda_i\), with every higher coefficient tautological. Never use cancellation in \(K_0(\mathrm{Var})\) as positivity; the proof must survive specialization to honest \(p\)-adic measures.
