+\(q(P)\) are nonzero.  Differentiating (3.1) at such a point gives
+
+\[
+[dg_2]=\lambda[dg_1],\qquad [dg_3]=\mu[dg_1],
+\tag{3.8}
+\]
+
+which explains both the rank and the measured ratios.  This is local
